---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import RelatedTools from '../../components/RelatedTools.astro';
import StudyNote from '../../components/StudyNote.astro';

const title = "5 Life-Saving Geometry Tricks Every Architect Uses Daily";
const description = "Discover the hidden mathematical shortcuts professionals use to calculate impossible angles in seconds.";
const image = "/images/blog/arch-tricks.png";

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: title,
  image: `https://webprotractor.netlify.app${image}`,
  description: description,
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Online Geometry Tools'
  }
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} schemas={[articleSchema]}>
  <ContentSection>
    <div class="w-full flex justify-center mb-8">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[
        { name: 'Blog', url: '/blog' },
        { name: 'Architecture Tricks', url: '/blog/5-life-saving-geometry-tricks' }
      ]} />
    </div>

    <article class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto">
      <header class="text-center mb-12">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="caption-mono text-[var(--color-link)] uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">Architecture Notes</span>
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-hairline-strong)]"></span>
          <span class="caption text-[var(--color-mute)]">Study Guide • Chapter 1</span>
        </div>
      </header>
      
      <StudyNote>
        <span class="study-sticker" style="top: -20px; right: 20px;">📌</span>
        
        <h1 style="margin-top: 0;">5 Life-Saving <span class="study-highlight">Geometry Tricks</span>!</h1>
        <p>Architects don't do hard math on site, they use <span class="study-underline">shortcuts</span>. Here is how they do it:</p>

        <div class="flex justify-center my-8">
          <svg width="24" height="60" viewBox="0 0 24 60" fill="none" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 5v50M5 45l7 10 7-10"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <h2>1. The 3-4-5 Rule (Builder's Square)</h2>
        <p>Need a perfect 90° angle? No protractor? No problem.</p>
        
        <div class="study-box">
          <span class="study-sticker" style="top: -25px; left: -20px;">💡</span>
          <h3>How it works:</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Measure <strong>3 ft</strong> down one wall.</li>
            <li>Measure <strong>4 ft</strong> down the other wall.</li>
            <li>If the diagonal is exactly <span class="study-highlight">5 ft</span>, you have a perfect square!</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">* Scales infinitely: 6-8-10, 30-40-50.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex justify-center my-8">
          <svg width="60" height="24" viewBox="0 0 60 24" fill="none" stroke="#e74c3c" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="transform: rotate(15deg);">
            <path d="M5 12h50M45 5l10 7-10 7"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <h2>2. The "1 in 60" Rule</h2>
        <p>This is for massive curves (like roads or stadiums).</p>
        <p>At <strong>60 units of distance</strong>, moving <strong>1 unit perpendicular</strong> equals exactly <span class="study-underline">1 degree</span>.</p>

        <h2>3. Digital Overlay 💻</h2>
        <p>Instead of printing massive blueprints, just screenshot the CAD file.</p>
        
        <div class="study-box" style="transform: rotate(1.5deg);">
          <span class="study-sticker" style="bottom: -20px; right: -20px;">📐</span>
          <h3>The Workflow:</h3>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6">
            <li>Open CAD file.</li>
            <li>Upload screenshot to an <a href="/online-protractor" class="text-blue-600 underline decoration-wavy">Online Protractor</a>.</li>
            <li>Overlay the glowing protractor.</li>
            <li>Read the exact measurement.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h2>4. The Golden Rectangle (Psychological Perfection)</h2>
        <p>Want a room to feel "perfect" to the human brain?</p>
        
        <div class="study-code">
          // The formula for aesthetic perfection:
          let shortWall = 10;
          let longWall = shortWall * 1.618;
          
          console.log(longWall); // 16.18 ft
        </div>
        
        <p>This creates a <span class="study-highlight">Golden Rectangle</span>. No complex drafting needed, just multiply by 1.618.</p>

        <h2>5. The Double-Check Mirror 🪞</h2>
        <p>When drawing symmetrical facades, the brain corrects errors automatically. To spot an angle that is off by 1°, hold the blueprint to a mirror.</p>
        <p><span class="study-underline">The asymmetry will instantly pop out.</span></p>

        <div class="flex justify-center mt-12 mb-4">
          <svg width="100" height="24" viewBox="0 0 100 24" fill="none" stroke="#555" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M10 12h80M10 12l10-7M10 12l10 7M90 12l-10-7M90 12l-10 7"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        
        <p class="text-center font-bold text-xl">Stop Guessing. Start Measuring.</p>

      </StudyNote>
    </article>
  </ContentSection>
  <RelatedTools currentPath="/blog/5-life-saving-geometry-tricks" />
</Layout>
